### ==============================================================================
### SOTP API Documentation & REST Client Collection
### ==============================================================================
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
### Click "Send Request" above any request or press Ctrl+Alt+R (Cmd+Alt+R on Mac).
### ==============================================================================

### Environment Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1
@contentType = application/json

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Authentication
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 Login (Default Demo Admin)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@sotp.local",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### Capture tokens from login response
@authToken = {{login.response.body.access_token}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.refresh_token}}

### 1.2 Refresh Access Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 1.3 Register New User
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "DevOps Engineer",
  "email": "devops@sotp.local",
  "password": "StrongPassword123!"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Device Management (Requires Authentication)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 List Devices (Paginated & Sorted)
GET {{baseUrl}}/devices/?limit=10&offset=0&sort_by=id&sort_order=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 2.2 Filter Devices by Type / Vendor / Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/devices/?limit=10&offset=0&device_type=router&vendor=cisco&is_active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 2.3 Create Device (Admin only)
# @name createDevice
POST {{baseUrl}}/devices/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "name": "core-router-01",
  "ip_address": "192.168.10.1",
  "device_type": "router",
  "vendor": "cisco",
  "model": "ISR-4331",
  "os_version": "IOS-XE 17.6",
  "location": "Warsaw-DC1-Rack4",
  "is_active": true,
  "credentials": {
    "snmp_community": "sotp_community",
    "ssh_username": "admin",
    "ssh_password": "DeviceSecretPassword123"
  }
}

### 2.4 Get Device by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/devices/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
